  "metadata": {
    "hosting": "hub-hosted Python adapter today",
    "state": "This is Forge's own management module for this service, not an integration with another system. An existing application was the example it is built from: the Python adapter holds the data contract taken from that example (sources, context mapping, record shapes). The module's own logic, storage and screens are not built.",
    "target": "A Go module built from the module SDK, with Python scripting for customization (owner, 2026-11-18). Its source path, language and template change in this spec when that code exists.",
    "time_contract_state": "The hub database mod_ims is declared as the rule the module is built to: every time it writes there comes from its own governed clock. The adapter does not use the database yet. M-4 to M-7 are run by the conformance kit through the Python transport, against a reference hub."
